## Overview

`editing-locale-switcher` provides a small form control for switching the active editing locale in multilingual forms. It is useful for forms that store localized fields in metadata or translation maps.

Set the active locale once with `KrakstackProvider`; pass `locale` directly only when a component needs an override. Message overrides are keyed by arbitrary locale strings, so additional languages can be supplied with `messages={{ es: { ... } }}`. Exact locale keys such as `es-MX` take precedence over base keys such as `es`; English is the final fallback.

## Features

- Arbitrary editing locale strings with English and French defaults
- Controlled `value` and `onValueChange` props
- Mobile-friendly icon label with desktop text
- In-file English and French labels with optional message overrides

## Usage

```tsx
import { EditingLocaleSwitcher, type EditingLocale } from "@/components/ui/editing-locale-switcher";
import { useState } from "react";

const [locale, setLocale] = useState<EditingLocale>("en");

<EditingLocaleSwitcher locale={uiLocale} value={locale} onValueChange={setLocale} />
<EditingLocaleSwitcher
  locale={uiLocale}
  locales={["en", "fr", "es"]}
  value={locale}
  onValueChange={setLocale}
  messages={{ en: { label: "Language", es: "Spanish" } }}
/>
```
